From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: profile manager CreateEmptyProfile, IWMProfile and IWMStreamConfig objects

Profile objects and CreateEmptyProfile, which had no objects behind it.

- IWMProfileManager::CreateEmptyProfile (versions 4.0, 7.0, 8.0, 9.0)
  returns a profile object implementing IWMProfile, IWMProfile2 and
  IWMProfile3: name, description, storage format (default V1), profile id
  (GUID_NULL for a profile made here), streams (GetStream, GetStreamByNumber,
  AddStream, RemoveStream*, ReconfigStream, CreateNewStream taking the lowest
  unused number 1..63; NS_E_NO_STREAM for an absent stream, NS_E_INVALID_STREAM
  for a duplicate number), mutual exclusions, bandwidth sharing, stream
  prioritization, GetExpectedPacketCount. Stream configurations are copies;
  their changes reach the profile through ReconfigStream or AddStream.
- IWMStreamConfig and IWMMediaProps objects (number 1..63, names, bitrate,
  buffer window (-1 when unset), media type with the ASF_E_BUFFERTOOSMALL size
  protocol); IWMMutualExclusion, IWMBandwidthSharing and
  IWMStreamPrioritization list objects. Removing a stream from a profile
  removes it from the lists.
- LoadProfileByID, LoadProfileByData, SaveProfile and the system profiles
  stay as they were (next patch / not available).

---
